# Expense Tracker (v1)

Personal, local-only money tracker. Not tax software, payroll, banking, or multi-user sync.

## In scope

- First-run onboarding (currency, budget, empty vs sample)
- Overview, ledger, recurring expenses, categories
- Monthly budget + display currency (optional per-month override)
- Browser SQLite via SQLocal / OPFS (Chromium)
- Android Chrome installable PWA + mobile shell (bottom tabs)
- HTTPS demo host (Vercel) with COEP/COOP headers
- TanStack Start / Router / Query + shadcn/ui (new-york) + Tailwind

## Out of scope for v1

- Capacitor / Expo / Play Store / App Store packaging (later phase)
- iOS Safari as a supported runtime (later: Capacitor + native SQLite)
- Cloud sync, accounts, auth, remote APIs
- Employer / tax / bank integrations

## Layout

| Path | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `src/app/` | Shell: gate, nav, theme, onboarding |
| `src/routes/` | Screens (Overview, Ledger, Recurring, Categories) |
| `src/components/ui/` | shadcn primitives |
| `src/components/layout/` | Page chrome (shell, header, empty/loading) |
| `src/components/` | Shared product widgets (charts, dialogs, stats) |
| `src/data/` | Repository, seed, sample ledger |
| `src/db/` | Drizzle schema + SQLocal client + migrator |
| `drizzle/` | Kit-generated SQL + `migrations.js` (commit these) |
| `src/lib/` | Domain helpers (`finance`, `types`, `transaction-defaults`, `backup`) |
| `src/lib/query/` | Query keys, invalidation, prefetch |
| `tests/unit/` | Vitest unit tests (keep out of `src/`) |

## Data

- All reads/writes go through `src/data/repository.ts`
- Schema in `src/db/schema.ts`; seed in `src/data/seed.ts`
- Schema changes: edit `schema.ts`, run `pnpm db:generate`, commit `drizzle/` — applied in-browser via `migrateSchema` (do not hand-write DDL)
- Invalidate TanStack Query keys from `src/lib/query/keys.ts` after mutations
- Amounts are numbers; format with `money(amount, currency)` from `src/lib/finance.ts`

## Imports

Use `#/` path aliases (e.g. `#/components/ui/button`, `#/app/app-nav`, `#/lib/query/keys`).
